// The name of every string the reader hears or sees, one line each.  What the
// strings say is in one file per language, i18n/<code>.def.
//
//   S(id)   a string
//   P(id)   a string with a number in it, in as many forms as the language
//           has plurals (see the language's file for its rule)
//
// A language file must give every id here and nothing else, or i18n.cpp does
// not compile (-Wswitch is an error there).  So an id is added here and in
// every language at once, and a language cannot ship with a hole in it.

P(kLines)

// model/transcript: block text.  Part of the transcript buffer, so also what
// is heard when arrowing over it.
S(kQuestionsMore)
S(kQuestionMultiSelect)
S(kFileLine)
S(kReplaceBefore)
S(kReplaceAfter)
S(kReplaceEverywhere)
S(kNewContent)
S(kDiff)
S(kLinesToLines)
S(kThinkingSummary)
S(kWritten)
S(kCreated)
S(kOutput)
S(kError)
S(kOutputEmpty)
S(kErrorEmpty)
S(kExpanded)
S(kInterrupted)
S(kToolDenied)
// The reader as a speaker, in front of every prompt in the transcript and in
// speech.  The agent's side is its own name ("claude: "), not translated.
S(kSpeakerUser)
// proto/: what the adapters say in the reader's language.  Mode labels are
// keys as well as text -- keys_dialog drops a mode whose label it has listed
// already, so two ids of the same mode (default, manual) must share a label.
S(kImage)
S(kToolDeclined)
S(kReasonRule)
S(kReasonSubcommands)
S(kModeNormal)
S(kModePlan)
S(kModePlanGloss)
S(kClaudeModeNormalGloss)
S(kClaudeModeAcceptEdits)
S(kClaudeModeAcceptEditsGloss)
S(kClaudeModeAuto)
S(kClaudeModeAutoGloss)
S(kClaudeModeBypass)
S(kClaudeModeBypassGloss)
S(kClaudeModeDontAsk)
S(kClaudeModeDontAskGloss)
S(kCodexModeNormalGloss)
S(kCodexModeReadOnly)
S(kCodexModeReadOnlyGloss)
S(kCodexModeFullAccess)
S(kCodexModeFullAccessGloss)
S(kCodexModeCustom)
S(kCodexModeCustomGloss)
// Block kinds, as navigation names them.
S(kKindPrompt)
S(kKindAnswer)
S(kKindDenied)
S(kKindInterrupted)
S(kKindThinking)
S(kKindTool)
S(kKindOutput)
